    "title": "QQ: Meaning, Gaming Slang Origin, and Tencent Messenger Guide",
    "slug": "qq-meaning-gaming-slang-origin-and-tencent-messenger-guide",
    "date": "Jul 26, 2026",
    "excerpt": "Uncover the dual meaning of QQ as a legendary gaming slang term for crying and Tencent's iconic Chinese messaging platform.",
    "body": "## What Does QQ Mean?\n\nFirst, many internet users recognize **QQ** as a popular emoticon representing crying eyes. In this context, the letter Q resembles a tearful eye. Therefore, typing \"QQ\" creates a face with tears streaming down both sides. Consequently, people send it to express sadness, disappointment, or exaggerated crying.\n\nIn addition, **QQ** holds a unique place in online gaming slang. Gamers often use the term to tell opponents to stop complaining. For example, when a player loses and complains in chat, others reply with \"QQ\" or \"QQ more.\"\n\n## The Origin of QQ in Gaming Slang\n\nInterestingly, the gaming usage started in the 1990s with Blizzard games like Warcraft II. In that game, players pressed **Alt + Q + Q** to quit the match immediately. Therefore, telling someone to \"QQ\" originally meant \"quit the game.\"\n\nOver time, players merged the quit shortcut with the crying emoticon. As a result, the phrase evolved into a double insult. Players now mock crybabies and tell them to leave the game simultaneously. For a deeper look at digital acronyms, check out our [whatsthatmean Dictionary](/) or explore our interactive [Slang & Acronym Quiz](/quiz).\n\n[AD]\n\n## QQ as Tencent's Iconic Messaging Platform\n\nBesides gaming slang, **QQ** represents Tencent QQ, one of China's most famous messaging services. Launched in 1999, Tencent QQ revolutionized instant communication across Asia. Furthermore, millions of users still log into QQ daily for messaging, file sharing, and social networking.\n\nFor official details on internet communication platforms, you can reference [Wikipedia's Overview](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tencent_QQ). You can also search for related messaging acronyms using our [Search \"QQ\"](/?search=QQ) feature or visit the [whatsthatmean Blog](/blog).\n\n## How to Use QQ in Everyday Communication\n\nYou can easily incorporate **QQ** into your online text chats or gaming lobbies. However, you should match your tone to the situation because context matters significantly.\n\nHere is a common scenario in online multiplayer games:\n\n> **Player A:** \"This game is so unfair, the lag is terrible and my team is awful!\"\n> **Player B:** \"Stop crying and QQ! Just play better next round.\"\n\nFurthermore, you can use the emoticon style in friendly text messages:\n\n> **Friend A:** \"I dropped my favorite ice cream cone on the sidewalk today...\"\n> **Friend B:** \"Oh no! QQ that is so sad!\"\n\nTo learn more about digital symbols, feel free to browse our [Emoji Dictionary](/emoji).\n\n[AD]\n\n## Frequently Asked Questions About QQ\n\n### Is QQ still popular today?\n\nYes, **QQ** remains active in both gaming slang and Chinese social media ecosystems.\n\n### Does QQ mean crying or quitting?\n\nOriginally, it meant quitting because of the key shortcut. However, modern users mostly use it as a crying emoticon or to mock complainers.\n\n### How do you pronounce QQ?\n\nYou simply pronounce it by saying the letter Q twice consecutively.",
